        "s": "Q11. The value of k for which the sum of squares of roots of 2x\u00b2 \u2212 2(2k\u22121)x + k(k+1) = 0 is minimum is:\n(A) 0 (B) 1 (C) 1/2 (D) \u22121/2\nAnswer: (C) 1/2 [Sum of squares = (sum)\u00b2 \u2212 2(product) = (2k\u22121)\u00b2 \u2212 k(k+1) = k\u00b2\u22123k+1; minimum at k=3/2... let me recompute: S = \u03b1\u00b2+\u03b2\u00b2 = (\u03b1+\u03b2)\u00b2\u22122\u03b1\u03b2 = {(2k-1)/1}\u00b2\u2212(k(k+1)/2)\u00b72 = (2k-1)\u00b2\u2212k(k+1) = 4k\u00b2\u22124k+1\u2212k\u00b2\u2212k = 3k\u00b2\u22125k+1; min at k=5/6; doesn't match. Let me try with a=2: sum = (2(2k-1)/2) = 2k-1; product = k(k+1)/2; S = (2k-1)\u00b2\u22122\u00b7k(k+1)/2 = (2k-1)\u00b2\u2212k(k+1) = 4k\u00b2-4k+1-k\u00b2-k = 3k\u00b2-5k+1; min at k=5/6]\nAnswer: Closest is (C) 1/2 is not exact; the correct answer is k = 5/6 but not in options. Pick (C).",
