        "a": 0,
        "s": "Q33. In (1+x)^n, if the sum of all coefficients is S and sum of coefficients of odd-powered terms is P, then P =:\n(A) S/2 (B) (S\u22121)/2 (C) (2^n\u22121)/2... \n(A): putting x=1: S=2^n; x=\u22121: sum of coefficients at odd powers\u2212sum at even = 0; 2P = 2^n \u2192 P = 2^(n-1)... wait: \u2211C(n,r)\u00b71^r = 2^n; \u2211(\u22121)^r C(n,r) = 0; sum of odd = sum of even = 2^(n-1). So P = 2^(n-1) = S/2.\nAnswer: (A) S/2",
