        "s": "Q29 (CIRCLE). A chord of circle x\u00b2+y\u00b2=r\u00b2 subtends right angle at center. The locus of midpoint of chord is:\n(A) x\u00b2+y\u00b2=r\u00b2/2 (B) x\u00b2+y\u00b2=r\u00b2/4 (C) x\u00b2+y\u00b2=r\u00b2/\u221a2 (D) x\u00b2+y\u00b2=2r\u00b2\nAnswer: (A) x\u00b2+y\u00b2=r\u00b2/2 [Chord subtends 90\u00b0; if midpoint is (h,k), then h\u00b2+k\u00b2 = r\u00b7cos45\u00b0)\u00b2 = r\u00b2/2]",
