        "s": "Q33. The focus of rectangular hyperbola xy=c\u00b2 are at:\n(A) (c\u221a2, c\u221a2) and (\u2212c\u221a2, \u2212c\u221a2) (B) (c\u221a2, 0) and (\u2212c\u221a2, 0)\n(C) Rotated version of (c,0) type (D) (c\u221a2, c\u221a2) only one focus\nAnswer: (A) (c\u221a2, c\u221a2) and (\u2212c\u221a2, \u2212c\u221a2) [Rotating x\u00b2-y\u00b2=2c\u00b2 by 45\u00b0: foci at (\u00b1c\u221a2, 0) become (\u00b1c, \u00b1c)... at rotation angle \u03c0/4: foci of x\u00b2-y\u00b2=2c\u00b2 are at (\u00b1c\u221a2\u00b7... xy=c\u00b2 is x\u00b2-y\u00b2=2c\u00b2 rotated; foci at (\u00b1c\u221a2, c\u221a2)? Let me: xy=c\u00b2; parametrize as x=c/t, y=ct; rotate 45\u00b0: X=(x+y)/\u221a2, Y=(y-x)/\u221a2; X=(c/t+ct)/\u221a2=c(t+1/t)/\u221a2; Y=(ct-c/t)/\u221a2=c(t-1/t)/\u221a2; X\u00b2-Y\u00b2=c\u00b2(t+1/t)\u00b2/2-c\u00b2(t-1/t)\u00b2/2=c\u00b2[(t+1/t)\u00b2-(t-1/t)\u00b2]/2=c\u00b2\u00b74/2=2c\u00b2; So in X,Y coordinates: X\u00b2-Y\u00b2=2c\u00b2; standard hyperbola with a\u00b2=2c\u00b2; foci at X=\u00b1a\u221a2=\u00b12c; in original: foci at X=2c, Y=0 \u2192 x=(X-Y)/\u221a2... hmm, foci of xy=c\u00b2 are at (\u00b1c\u221a2, \u00b1c\u221a2)?... After rotation: foci at (X=2c, Y=0) and (-2c,0) in rotated frame; unrotating: x=(X+Y)/\u221a2... Let me just state: foci at (c\u221a2, c\u221a2) and (-c\u221a2, -c\u221a2)]\nAnswer: (A)",
