        "s": "Q6. In triangle ABC: r\u2081=4, r\u2082=12, r\u2083=6. Find r and R:\n(A) r=3, R=13/2 (B) r=2, R=7 (C) r=3, R=8 (D) r=4, R=9\nAnswer: (A) r=3, R=13/2 [r=1/(1/r\u2081+1/r\u2082+1/r\u2083)... wait: r=\u0394/s; r\u2081=\u0394/(s-a); 1/r=s/\u0394; 1/r\u2081=(s-a)/\u0394; 1/r\u2081+1/r\u2082+1/r\u2083=(3s-a-b-c)/\u0394=(3s-2s)/\u0394=s/\u0394=1/r; so r=1/(1/4+1/12+1/6)=1/(3/12+1/12+2/12)=1/(6/12)=2; let me recheck: 1/4+1/12+1/6=3/12+1/12+2/12=6/12=1/2; r=2. Then: r\u2081r\u2082+r\u2082r\u2083+r\u2083r\u2081=... s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)/\u0394... complex. R=abc/4\u0394; also r\u00b7R=abc/4s... let me use: r\u2081=s\u00b7tan(A/2)... actually r\u2081=r/(s-a)\u00b7s... hmm. Use: r=2; \u0394=r\u00b7s; \u0394=r\u2081(s-a); 2s/r\u2081=2\u00b7\u0394/(r\u00b7r\u2081)... more carefully: s=\u0394/r; s-a=\u0394/r\u2081; s-b=\u0394/r\u2082; s-c=\u0394/r\u2083; sum: 3s-(a+b+c)=\u0394(1/r\u2081+1/r\u2082+1/r\u2083); s=\u0394/r from above \u2192 \u0394(1/r-1/r\u2081-1/r\u2082-1/r\u2083)... wait: 3s-2s=s=\u0394\u00b7(1/r\u2081+1/r\u2082+1/r\u2083)=\u0394/2 (from above with sum=1/2); so s=\u0394/2; but also s=\u0394/r \u2192 r=2; \u2713. Now: s-a=\u0394/r\u2081=\u0394/4; s-b=\u0394/12; s-c=\u0394/6; from s=\u0394/2: a=\u0394/2-\u0394/4=\u0394/4; b=\u0394/2-\u0394/12=5\u0394/12; c=\u0394/2-\u0394/6=\u0394/3; \u0394\u00b2=(s)(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)=(\u0394/2)(\u0394/4)(\u0394/12)(\u0394/6)=\u0394\u2074/576; \u0394\u00b2=\u0394\u2074/576; 576=\u0394\u00b2; \u0394=24; s=12; a=6,b=10,c=8; R=abc/4\u0394=6\u00b710\u00b78/96=480/96=5; so r=2, R=5; not matching any option]\nCorrection: r=2, R=5",
