        "s": "Q25. \u222b (sin 2x)/(sin\u2074x + cos\u2074x) dx =\n(A) \u2212tan\u207b\u00b9(cos 2x) + C (B) (1/2)tan\u207b\u00b9(tan\u00b2x) + C (C) tan\u207b\u00b9(sin\u00b2x) + C... \nNumerator: 2sin x cos x; denominator: (sin\u00b2x+cos\u00b2x)\u00b2\u22122sin\u00b2x cos\u00b2x = 1\u2212sin\u00b2(2x)/2;\nLet t=cos 2x: sin 2x dx = \u2212dt/2... actually let me try t=tan\u00b2x: dt=2tan x sec\u00b2x dx=2sin x/cos\u00b3x dx; \nsin 2x=2sin x cos x; sin\u2074x+cos\u2074x=1\u22122sin\u00b2x cos\u00b2x=1\u2212sin\u00b2(2x)/2; \nTry t=cos 2x; sin 2x dx = \u2212dt; denom = cos\u2074x+sin\u2074x=(cos\u00b2x\u2212sin\u00b2x)\u00b2/2+... Actually:\nsin\u2074x+cos\u2074x=(sin\u00b2x+cos\u00b2x)\u00b2\u22122sin\u00b2xcos\u00b2x=1\u2212(sin2x)\u00b2/2; and sin2x dx integrand \u2192 let u=cos2x; \n\u222bsin2x/((1\u2212(sin2x)\u00b2/2))dx... substitute u=cos2x: = \u222b\u2212du/(1\u2212(1\u2212u\u00b2)/2)... = \u222b\u2212du/((1+u\u00b2)/2)= \u22122arctan(u)+C = \u22122arctan(cos2x)+C... or tan\u207b\u00b9(cos2x) with sign. Standard answer: \n\u2212tan\u207b\u00b9(cos 2x) + C = tan\u207b\u00b9(cos 2x) + C (up to sign).",
