        "q": "\u222b\u2080^(\u03c0/2) sin x cos x/(sin x+cos x)\u00b2 dx =\nLet I; use substitution x\u2192\u03c0/2\u2212x: I'=\u222bsin x cos x/(sin x+cos x)\u00b2dx = same; also note 2I=\u222b(2sin x cos x)/(sin x+cos x)\u00b2dx = \u222bsin 2x/(sin x+cos x)\u00b2dx... careful analysis gives I=1/2... \nHmm actually: (sinx+cosx)\u00b2=1+sin2x; \u222bsin2x/(1+sin2x)\u00b7(1/2)dx... =1/2\u222b[1\u22121/(1+sin2x)]dx; \n\u222b\u2080^(\u03c0/2) 1/(1+sin2x)dx = [\u22121/2\u00b7cot(x+\u03c0/4)]\u2080^(\u03c0/2)... \nStandard result:",
